# Chinese Writing Voice

Use this rule when producing or editing Chinese prose that a reader will consume: reports, memos, proposals, reviews, long responses, slide notes, or stable AI-facing docs.

Invoke `hoveath-chinese-writing-voice`.

Default voice:
- direct, concrete, judgment-oriented
- no formulaic praise or filler
- no ornate adjectives or marketing language
- no emotional em dash pauses
- technical identifiers stay in backticks

Chinese prose should sound written in Chinese, not translated line by line from English.
